id: intl/locales/options/0001
area: intl
op: Intl.Locale (variants option)
in: str:"en" str:"\u212Aaaaa"
out: error: RangeError
class: normative
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl-locale-constructor spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-updatelanguageid overruled:intlref@1=value:str:"en"
script: new Intl.Locale("en", {variants: "\u212aaaaa"}).toString()
note: row L14: the variants option must be variant subtags, ASCII, so a KELVIN SIGN is refused; Intl.Locale's UpdateLanguageId reads the variants option and throws a RangeError unless it is a sequence of unicode_variant_subtag; the reference does not read the option at all (V8's --js-intl-locale-variants is off by default) (the reference answered str:"en")
since: 27

id: intl/locales/options/0002
area: intl
op: Intl.Locale (numberingSystem option)
in: str:"en" str:"\u212Ahmr"
out: error: RangeError
class: normative
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl-locale-constructor ref:intlref@1
script: new Intl.Locale("en", {numberingSystem: "\u212ahmr"}).toString()
note: row L14: an option value must be ASCII type subtags; a letter culture casing folds into ASCII is refused
since: 27

